m with LR=0.5 typically leads to:\n- Rapid initial convergence (epochs 0-8 show this)\n- Subsequent oscillation/instability when approaching minima\n- Potential model divergence or plateau (which matches the observed behavior)\n\n**Recommended fix**: Reduce learning rate to a standard range (0.001-0.01).\n\n### Evidence Summary\n1. **metrics.jsonl**: val_acc stuck at 0.753059 for epochs 9-19 (11 epochs with identical value to 6 decimal places)\n2. **metrics.jsonl**: train_loss spike and oscillation in epochs 9-11 (0.583 \u2192 0.730 \u2192 0.562)\n3. **config.yaml**: lr=0.5 is extremely high for Adam optimizer\n4. **logs/stdout.log**: Confirms pattern - validation accuracy frozen after epoch 9",
